## Summary

Consistency audit of main at 30e7741. The goal was to fix wording that would mislead a reader of the schema, the docs, or the screens, without changing behavior.

What landed: schema and docs/datamodel.md now match the code. MEMBER.member of excluded is someone a manager keeps off an email list, or someone taken off a guest list, not a Loop unsubscribe (an unsubscribe stays a member of the list's unsubscribed group). GROUP.name and the datamodel rename sentence include Audience and Hidden groups, and RULE.under skips audience groups, matching the rename trigger and servingColumns.

Ian then asked for the screen labels that had been left alone. HCA-Team sentences that said "organizers" now say "co-chairs", and the category approval choice says "a co-chair approves" instead of "an admin approves". The person card and the family card say "Open Helios Who?", matching the birthday card.

Decisions: correct the descriptions rather than change membership or renames, because the code was already right. Use "co-chairs" rather than "the co-chairs and the Team admins" because Ian chose the shorter phrase after being told Team admins also approve and see hidden lists; it matches the Chair and Co-Chairs heading. A review finding that the exclusive sentences leave Team admins out was ignored for that reason. One directory link, "Open Helios Who?", rather than "Profile" on a person and "on" on a family, because a family page is not a profile.

Left out: When and Celebrate still say an admin approves, because an admin of that app is who approves there. The volunteer-settings hint that says "chairs" was not in the agreed list. Merging main was already up to date. go build ./... passed. The full test suite failed once on TestWikiShareHeader and passed on a rerun of internal/db and of ./...; that test does not touch these wording changes.

